"""
Tutorial 9a — survey the flight envelope.

Trims and linearizes the aircraft at 100 × 100 flight conditions. `Envelope` shows how the
trimmed angle of attack, thrust, elevator and pitch divergence rate change with airspeed
and altitude, and the grid of step 9b's controllers: one scheduling variable is not enough
across this range.
"""
analysis TutorialEnvelope
  extends F16ModelWorkshop.EnvelopeAnalysis(velocities = [140.0, 250.0], altitudes = [0.0, 9000.0], points = 100)
  model = F16ModelWorkshop.Plant.F16PlantModel()
end

"""
Tutorial 9b — fly the envelope-scheduled MPC.

`FlightResponse` shows both references tracked, the angle of attack against the trimmed
angle of attack interpolated in the grid, and how many of the grid's controllers the
flight has built.
"""
analysis TutorialEnvelopeMPC
  extends F16ModelWorkshop.FlightAnalysis(stop = 80.0, panels = ["Airspeed (m/s): f16plant.vt, vt_reference", "Altitude (m): f16plant.alt, alt_reference", "Angle of attack and the trimmed angle of attack interpolated in the grid (rad): f16plant.alpha, alpha_ref.y", "Grid controllers built so far: optimizer.built", "Elevator (deg): f16plant.el", "Thrust (N): f16plant.T", "Solver status, 1 when every active controller solved: optimizer.exitflag"])
  model = EnvelopeMPCDemo()
end

"""
Tutorial 9c — rebuild the grid's trim table.

Re-trims the aircraft at the nodes of `assets/envelope_trim_alpha.csv` and rewrites it. To
move or refine the grid, edit the table's first column (airspeeds) or header row
(altitudes), then run this.
"""
analysis TutorialEnvelopeTable
  extends F16ModelWorkshop.EnvelopeAnalysis(velocities = [140.0, 250.0], altitudes = [0.0, 9000.0], points = 2, table_dir = "assets")
  model = F16ModelWorkshop.Plant.F16PlantModel()
end
